 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon Comprehend API (2017-11-27). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Flywheels are stored ACTIVE configuration for a new model: no data lake is created in the DataLakeS3Uri bucket, no dataset is ingested and no iteration trains, evaluates or promotes a model, so LatestFlywheelIteration and ActiveModelArn stay absent. ActiveModelArn is refused on CreateFlywheel and UpdateFlywheel because no trained document classifier or entity recognizer exists; TaskConfig must carry the configuration of its ModelType, and UpdateFlywheel changes only DataAccessRoleArn (DataSecurityConfig is refused). ListFlywheels is not implemented because its FlywheelSummary list differs from the FlywheelProperties description; use DescribeFlywheel with the flywheel ARN. Detection, classification and every analysis job, document classifiers and entity recognizers (which train), endpoints (which need a trained model), datasets, flywheel iterations, model import and resource policies return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501.",
  "title": "Amazon Comprehend (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2017-11-27"
 },
